    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The complement of $Y,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{Y},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $Y.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the letters $a$ through $z,$ while the set $Y$ consists of the letters $a$ through $j.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $Y$ are the letters $k$ through $z.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{Y}=\\{k,l,m,…,z\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "d9017d39d5fb32438ffb5c19debbe5022d012d96d81b1ecfb368a1d4c8d8882e",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
